  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Perfect Trading Co vs Commissioner Of Customs & Ors on 12 December, 2024 Author: Prathiba M. Singh Bench: Prathiba M. Singh, Amit Sharma $~42 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + M/S Perfect Trading Co. Through: Mr Sambhav Singh, Advs versus Commissioner Of Customs & Ors. Through: Mr. Aditya & Mr. Inde Coram: Justice Prathiba M. Singh Justice Amit Sharma Order % 12.12.2024 1.",
    "facts": "2. The present petition has been filed seeking a writ in the nature of mandamus for release of consignment of roasted Areca Nuts which have been imported by the Petitioner. 3. There are conflicting test reports on record with respect to the Areca Nuts traded by the Petitioner company. Some of the tests say that the Areca Nuts have moisture content and also are infested by mould/ insects and hence not fit for human consumption. However, the test reports filed by the Petitioner state the contrary and state that the tests show that the moisture content is well within the prescribed limits, thus refuting the claim of excessive moisture. 4. Considering the contradictions in the test reports, and in order to have an independent assessment of the goods, let The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) depute a food inspector for inspection of the This is a digitally signed order. The authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. The Customs Officials and the Petitioner's Representatives may accompany the officials from FSSAI for the purpose of assessment of goods.",
